{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791284555,"nonce":"PGppKlzQzk8cQkZDBfYFUdNKW7w=","title":"Convert enum constructor arguments to their payload field types","message":"Issue5486 stores a Dynamic Int box in an Option\u003cInt\u003e.Some payload. Both qualified and bare enum constructor lowering copy argument registers directly, so literal patterns compare a box address with the expected Int. Generic constructors inferred from Dynamic arguments also need the destination type arguments at typed initializers, assignments, and returns.\n\nNormalize both constructor forms through the same writer. Resolve field types using the concrete destination for the same enum, scope that destination separately to each nested argument, apply optional/Dynamic boxing or unboxing, promote Int arguments to Float when required, and write complete 8-byte slots. Readers retain the declared field representation.\n\nThe independent EnumDynamicPayloads regression also exposes haxe_enum_get_parameters boxing String/reference payload addresses as Int values. Use the existing field boxing helper so enum reflection returns the correct Dynamic tags and preserves nullable boxes.\n\nRegression coverage: both constructor forms; Dynamic Int/Float/Bool/String inputs; generic concrete destinations; Null\u003cDynamic\u003e inputs; literal patterns; typed returns; nested constructors consumed as Option\u003cFloat\u003e; Int-to-Float promotion; nullable and Dynamic payloads; Type.enumParameters for primitive fields. The original fixture fails at Int payload on the prior checkpoint, printing the box address instead of -10.\n\nRelated broader issue: 4f791be88d3ec9ca0e2a0b96f3c3e5524b74f435e1aecc2c14199e0c6b0ba653. Generic enum equality and nested generic pattern inference remain separate defects.","files":null}]}